  fix (review): move the expressions into the env of the step, and read the variables where they were, quoted as the shell needs (bash and sh)  [--fix=review]
    side effect: The value of the ${{ }} expression is no longer parsed by the program that reads the script (the shell, or the JavaScript runtime of actions/github-script) as part of the script text: characters of the value that the program interpreted before the fix (such as $, `, \, double quotes and line breaks) are taken as plain characters, and a workflow that relied on the program interpreting those characters runs differently.

